---

import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Photographs, writing, and experiments in AI.">
  <p>
    In the Summer of 2025, I was hospitalized for approaching perfection.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is where I share photographs, writing, and experiments in AI.
  </p>
  <p>
    All photographs are actually for free. I will mail you one. Just give me your
    mailing address via the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, and I will mail you a photo.
  </p>
  <section class="about-process">
    <p>
      A note on process, because this form of expression is a little different for me.
      It starts with pen and paper. I bullet out the theme and the hooks rattling around
      in my head, then I read the page back and connect them out loud, dictating the essay
      into the plain text editor I use for work, which is Sublime Text (shout out to
      Sublime Text. I&rsquo;ve been using you for eighteen years, and I&rsquo;ve never paid for you).
      I move that into Microsoft Word, and then I type more and edit what I spoke. Finally
      I run it through Grammarly, because I can&rsquo;t spell. I think I have a dusting of
      dyslexia&hellip;undiagnosed, but likely.
    </p>
    <p>The photos are mine. Some of the art is MidJourney.</p>
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m calling this &ldquo;brazed writing&rdquo;: the bullets are the jig that holds the pieces in
      position, the spoken draft is the parent metal, never melted, and the edits are the
      filler pulled into the joints. Essentially, I&rsquo;m converting the ideas in my head into
      text using modern technology.
    </p>
    <p>
      I&rsquo;ve worked in corporate innovation for eleven and a half years. I have advised
      innovation labs and R&amp;D departments, probably over 200 of them in my career.
      I&rsquo;m just taking my own advice with this new method.
    </p>
  </section>

  <blockquote class="about-quote">
    <p>&ldquo;There was that law of life, so cruel and so just, that one must grow or else pay more for remaining the same.&rdquo;</p>
    <cite>&mdash; Norman Mailer, 1955, <em>The Deer Park</em></cite>
  </blockquote>
  <img src="/about-dogs.jpg" alt="The author's two dogs sharing an armchair" class="about-photo" />
  <p class="meta">
    Matthew R. Kenney lives in Bloomfield, New Jersey, with his wife, three children, and two dogs
    with PTSD. He is Catholic, and he is working on it.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.about-process {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .about-process p {
    margin: 0 0 0.875rem;
  }

  .about-process p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-quote {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .about-quote p {
    margin: 0 0 0.375rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .about-quote cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .about-photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin: 2rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
